.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=RTF View
.Options CtrlColorChar=\

@Contents
$ #RTF View#
    Plugin RTF View is intended for viewing .rtf files in the
form of the normal text with colors. The plugin does not use
external libraries for transformation, and contains built in parser.

           (c) Vladimir Valikayev
 \0Fлллллллл\-  ~http://triv.fromru.com~@http://triv.fromru.com@, ~http://vtriv.narod.ru~@http://vtriv.narod.ru@
 \01лллллллл\-  [triv]{@@}[fromru].[com]
 \04лллллллл\-  2:5005/14.141

   ~Plugin usage~@Syntax@
   ~Configuring RTF View~@Config@

@Syntax
$ #RTF View usage

    You can use plugin as follows::
 #-# open .rtf file for editing (F4) and choose #RTF View# from the plugin
commands list (F11);
 #-# from the command line, for example:
      #rtfv#:somefile.rtf

    I have added association of .rtf files for Alt+F3 combination:
      #rtfv:!\!.!#

    When the file opens, its format is checked and if it not the .rtf file,
it is simply ignored, any message is not deduced.


  Look also: ~Contents~@Contents@  ~Configuring RTF View~@Config@

@Config
$ #Configuring RTF View#

 #[ ] Show document's info at the end of file#


 In the end of the file the information on the document will be deduced,
for example:

 \78Title   : Help                    \-
 \78Subject :                         \-
 \78Author  : Vladimir Valikayev      \-
 \78Manager :                         \-
 \78Company : TrivLab                 \-
 \78Operator: Triv                    \-
 \78Create time  : 24/08/2005 18:49:00\-
 \78Print time   :                    \-
 \78Revision time: 26/08/2005 15:34:00\-
 \78Backup time  :                    \-


 #[ ] Use colors#

 If you switch off, the text will be deduced \70black on grey\- and used in the .rtf file
colors will be ignored.

  \00 \-  #Tab size#

 The size of tabulation.


  Look also: ~Contents~@Contents@
